      "content": "To stay ahead of those sneaky, hidden risks, you need to practice \"security hygiene,\" which is basically constant vigilance. This means regularly updating all your software—your website platform, plugins, and any payment processors—because updates often patch those little vulnerabilities. It's a proactive approach, like constantly checking the perimeter of your shop, not just waiting for a big smash-and-grab. You should also limit who has access to the backend of your shop; only essential staff should have those keys.",
